  <main_text>
    <l n="1">„quòd jungatur cum observatione Sab-</l>
    <l n="2">„bathorum selectio certorum ciborum, „</l>
    <l n="3">Rom. xiv, 5, &amp;seq. tùm quòd sermo</l>
    <l n="4">„sit de illâ dierum æstimatione quâ offen-</l>
    <l n="5">„debantur Christiani, Rom. xiv, 1, &amp;</l>
    <l n="6">„seqq. <i>Hæc verò diei Dominicæ observationi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="7">
      <i>„accommodare qui volet,</i> infantiam suam,</l>
    <l n="8">„aut, si mavis, malitiam, nimium prodit.</l>
    <l n="9">„Nam nec die Dominicâ certi cibi ufur-</l>
    <l n="10">„pantur, nec die Dominicâ ab Ecclesiâ</l>
    <l n="11">„Apostolicâ offendi possunt Christiani.</l>
    <l n="12">„II. <i>Ad egena mundi elementa regredi hos,</i>
    </l>
    <l n="13">
      <i>„qui dies certos observant,</i> Gal. iv, 10, 11.</l>
    <l n="14">„Verùm hoc loco de illâ tantùm dierum</l>
    <l n="15">„observatione agitur, quæ evacuat Euan-</l>
    <l n="16">„gelii efficaciam. Jàm verò diei Domini-</l>
    <l n="17">„cæ observatio virtutem seu efficaciam</l>
    <l n="18">„Euangelii non evacuat; Alias Apostoli-</l>
    <l n="19">„ca Ecclesia eam observâsset. (Lege,non</l>
    <l n="20">„observâsset). III. <i>Non esse damnandum</i>
    </l>
    <l n="21">
      <i>„quenquam respectu festi, novilunii, aut</i>
    </l>
    <l n="22">
      <i>„Sabbathorum,quæ sunt umbra rerum futu-</i>
    </l>
    <l n="23">
      <i>„rarum;</i> Col. ii, 16, 17. At hîc disserit</l>
    <l n="24">„Apostolus de Sabbathis, quæ suntum-</l>
    <l n="25">„bra rerum futurarum; dies autem Do-</l>
    <l n="26">„minica non est umbra rerum futurarum; „sed</l>
